messages.content:
**Task A: Adaptive Path Scheduling**

Create a new, structured learning path based on the learner's profile.
The number of sessions should be within [1, 10]; if the requested count falls
outside that range, clamp it to the nearest bound.

* **Learner Profile**: {
  "learner_information": "Marketing analyst with three years of experience in Excel-based reporting and Tableau dashboards; holds a BSc in Business Administration; has written small Python scripts to clean CSV exports. Strong practical data experience in marketing/business analytics, now transitioning to a junior data scientist role. Familiar with business KPIs, campaign measurement, and dashboarding; new to formal programming-based analytics, statistics, and ML.",
  "learning_goal": "Leverage my marketing analyst background (Excel, Tableau, basic Python scripting) to transition into a junior data scientist role within a year by mastering Python-based data analysis (Pandas, NumPy), SQL for querying business data, and applied statistics for marketing and business analytics.",
  "cognitive_status": {
    "overall_progress": 60,
    "mastered_skills": [
      {
        "name": "Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)",
        "proficiency_level": "intermediate"
      },
      {
        "name": "Data Visualization with Matplotlib & Seaborn",
        "proficiency_level": "beginner"
      }
    ],
    "in_progress_skills": [
      {
        "name": "Python Programming for Data Analysis",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Data Wrangling with Pandas",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Numerical Computing with NumPy",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "unlearned"
      },
      {
        "name": "SQL Querying for Business Data",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Applied Statistics for Business & Marketing Analytics",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Hypothesis Testing & A/B Experimentation",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Regression Analysis & Predictive Modeling",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "unlearned"
      },
      {
        "name": "Foundational Machine Learning Concepts",
        "required_proficiency_level": "beginner",
        "current_proficiency_level": "unlearned"
      }
    ]
  },
  "learning_preferences": {
    "content_style": "Detailed explanations with practical, marketing-grounded examples; concise summaries provided for review",
    "activity_type": "Interactive exercises and hands-on querying; prefers applying concepts to real business datasets over passive reading",
    "additional_notes": "Learns best when new skills connect to prior Excel/Tableau experience (e.g., mapping Pandas operations to Excel workflows, SQL to BI data pulls). Recommend project-based learning using marketing datasets to reinforce engagement and career relevance."
  },
  "behavioral_patterns": {
    "system_usage_frequency": "Average of 3 logins per week (assumed initially; to be updated as usage data accumulates)",
    "session_duration_engagement": "Sessions average 30 minutes; high engagement observed in interactive tasks",
    "motivational_triggers": "Motivational message triggered due to decreased login frequency last week; encourage consistent study cadence and milestone celebrations tied to the one-year career transition goal",
    "additional_notes": "Career-change motivation is a strong driver; short, goal-oriented sessions with visible progress tracking recommended to sustain momentum. Monitor for irregular login patterns and prompt with adaptive nudges if engagement dips."
  }
}
* **Desired Session Count**: 5

text:
{
    "learning_path": [
        {
            "id": "Session 1",
            "title": "Spreadsheet to Script: Python & Pandas Foundations with Marketing Data",
            "abstract": "Begin your transition by translating what you already know from Excel into Python. Detailed explanations map every concept to familiar workflows: DataFrames are your Excel tables, filtering rows is your AutoFilter, and .groupby() is your PivotTable. You'll set up a Python environment, master variables, loops, and functions, then load real marketing campaign CSV exports into Pandas to clean, filter, and sort data just as you would in a spreadsheet. Learning is hands-on: short 30-minute interactive coding challenges use actual campaign and customer datasets, each followed by a concise summary for quick review. The session milestone—rebuilding one of your existing Excel campaign reports entirely in Pandas—delivers visible progress toward your data scientist goal and celebrates your first career-transition win.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["Python Programming for Data Analysis", "Data Wrangling with Pandas"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "Python Programming for Data Analysis", "level": "intermediate"},
                {"name": "Data Wrangling with Pandas", "level": "intermediate"}
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "Session 2",
            "title": "NumPy & Advanced Pandas: Power Tools for Marketing Data Wrangling",
            "abstract": "Level up from spreadsheet thinking to programmatic analytics. This session introduces NumPy arrays—think of them as supercharged Excel ranges built for speed—and shows how vectorized operations replace repetitive formulas. In Pandas, you'll go deeper: merging datasets (like VLOOKUP/XLOOKUP, but scalable), reshaping with pivot and melt (your PivotTable, supercharged), time-based resampling of weekly campaign metrics, and writing custom functions with apply(). Every hands-on exercise uses realistic marketing data: joining web analytics with CRM exports, calculating rolling conversion rates, and aggregating channel performance. Detailed walkthroughs connect each operation to the Excel/Tableau workflow you already know, and concise cheat-sheet summaries make review painless. You'll finish with a toolkit that handles in seconds what once took hours of manual spreadsheet work.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["Numerical Computing with NumPy", "Data Wrangling with Pandas"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "Numerical Computing with NumPy", "level": "intermediate"}
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "Session 3",
            "title": "SQL for Business Data: From BI Data Pulls to Direct Queries",
            "abstract": "Stop waiting for pre-built extracts—query business databases directly. This session teaches SQL by connecting it to what you already know: SELECT statements are like choosing Tableau columns, JOINs are your VLOOKUP across tables, and GROUP BY is your pivot aggregation. Through interactive, hands-on querying labs against a realistic e-commerce and marketing database (orders, campaigns, customers, web sessions), you'll progress from basic SELECT and WHERE clauses to aggregations, multi-table JOINs, subqueries, and CASE-based funnel segmentation. Each concept includes a detailed, marketing-grounded explanation and a concise summary for review. The capstone challenge: answer three real business questions—customer lifetime value by acquisition channel, campaign ROI by region, and weekly retention—by writing queries a junior data scientist would be proud of.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["SQL Querying for Business Data"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "SQL Querying for Business Data", "level": "intermediate"}
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "Session 4",
            "title": "Applied Statistics & A/B Testing: Experiment Like a Marketing Scientist",
            "abstract": "Turn intuition into evidence. Building on your Pandas skills, this session covers the statistics that power business decisions: distributions, sampling, confidence intervals, and correlation versus causation—all illustrated with marketing examples such as email open rates, ad conversions, and seasonal sales. The core focus is hypothesis testing for A/B experiments: framing null and alternative hypotheses, choosing the right test (t-test, chi-square, proportion tests), computing statistical significance and power, and calculating required sample sizes before launch. You'll run interactive experiments end-to-end in Python on simulated campaign A/B test data and learn to interpret p-values like a scientist rather than a dashboard consumer. Concise summaries follow each concept for fast review. Milestone: design and fully analyze an A/B test for a fictional email campaign.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["Applied Statistics for Business & Marketing Analytics", "Hypothesis Testing & A/B Experimentation"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "Applied Statistics for Business & Marketing Analytics", "level": "intermediate"},
                {"name": "Hypothesis Testing & A/B Experimentation", "level": "intermediate"}
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "Session 5",
            "title": "Regression & Predictive Modeling: Marketing Analytics Capstone",
            "abstract": "Close your path with the predictive skills that define data science. You'll build your first models with scikit-learn: linear regression to forecast marketing spend impact, logistic regression to predict customer churn and conversion, plus foundational machine learning concepts—train/test splits, overfitting, and evaluation metrics like R², RMSE, and classification accuracy. Everything connects to your growing toolkit: feature engineering with Pandas, visuals with Matplotlib and Seaborn, and insights delivered in clear business language. The capstone is a project-based, portfolio-ready analysis on a real marketing dataset—segment customers, model conversion drivers, and present predictions with compelling visualizations. Detailed explanations keep you grounded, concise summaries lock in learning, and completing this capstone is a milestone worth celebrating on your one-year journey to junior data scientist.",
            "if_learned": false,
            "associated_skills": ["Regression Analysis & Predictive Modeling", "Foundational Machine Learning Concepts", "Data Visualization with Matplotlib & Seaborn"],
            "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
                {"name": "Regression Analysis & Predictive Modeling", "level": "intermediate"},
                {"name": "Foundational Machine Learning Concepts", "level": "beginner"}
            ]
        }
    ]
}
